{
 "about": "Finds out in the game whether mechanism assets the official samples never touch have a preset status under the id the others follow, (asset id - 4000) x 10, and what values 1 and 2 do. scene_add_prefab registers the guessed id (presetStatusId); an id the asset does not have makes the editor's playtest check fail and name the prefab, so the wrong guesses were taken out one playtest at a time. As it stands (2026-10-11): five of the thirty-two have no such id and carry none here (10005023, 10005093, 10005142, 10006001, 10006002); the other twenty-seven take value 1, two of them also value 2 (knowledge/notes/preset-status.zh-CN.md). Four things at a time in front of the camera, six seconds each group: value 0, then 1, then 2, read back each time. One graph is shared by all thirty-two prefabs. Prints: PS_READY, PS_GROUP n, PS_V <asset> <value> (twice per thing: after setting 1, after setting 2), PS_CHANGED <asset>.",
